<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ed Sheeran calls Gaza war catastrophic after dropping Macklemore over pro-Palestinian comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cffd0b7d8f76046860e92395d5e4bbf92bda380154328c3abe2a584cecd0d7c8</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:57:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-war-catastrophic-after-dropping-macklemore-over-pro-palestinian-comments" /><summary type="html">English singer Ed Sheeran opened his first show since his opener Macklemore was dropped after making pro-Palestinian comments onstage. The move sparked controversy and prompted several other support acts to drop out of the tour, publishing statements citing their support for Palestinians. While some concert goers could be seen trying to sell their tickets on Saturday, others have voiced their support for the 'Shape of You' singer. Story by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Three media outlets barred from the White House over 'fake news'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16ace124d067522940cf028388b72009089065b005611763a8f4fa81e554f8e7</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:55:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/three-media-outlets-barred-from-the-white-house-over-fake-news" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has suggested that more news outlets may be barred from the White House after he announced he was banning Politico, CNN and MS NOW. On Saturday, all three outlets said that the White House confiscated their teams' press passes; they have also hinted at legal action. The ban has come under sharp criticism from press freedom advocates, as Charlotte Hughes explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>US and Denmark reach Greenland security deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:101823ca1e55c09313ac5f5ed1585f6d08b7b69566de60f5e65964e6a568a3b6</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:40:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-greenland-security-deal" /><summary type="html">The US and Denmark have announced a deal on Greenland's security, resolving a diplomatic dispute sparked by President Donald Trump when he threatened to seize the semi-autonomous territory. The exact terms of the deal remain uncertain but it seems Denmark will maintain its sovereignty while the US will be able to develop a significant military presence on the island, and ban their adversaries from building their own bases on the island. Details by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentines protest Milei's austerity, demanding higher wages and public spending</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c90a4b15e0f596599595f2baf839947ea0e6c8611b287bd3aaf5081e348aecd</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:38:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/argentines-protest-milei-s-austerity-demanding-higher-wages-and-public-spending" /><summary type="html">Tensions are boiling over in Argentina, where a massive wave of public anger is spilling onto the streets of the capital. Following months of aggressive economic reforms and rising household debt, hundreds took to the streets in a "March of Anger", targeting President Javier Milei's austerity agenda. Details by Caitlin Brown.</summary></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico reporters blocked from White House after Trump ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e2029430f299fa8a39b5398f8e36a4bed97dafc4e25a314cc27a824e7cda072</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T17:02:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cnn-ms-now-politico-reporters-blocked-from-white-house-after-trump-ban--a8c3f3f48609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cnn-ms-now-politico-reporters-blocked-from-white-house-after-trump-ban" /><summary type="html">White House correspondents for CNN, MS NOW and Politico on Saturday were blocked from entering the US president's office and residence a day after President Donald Trump announced he was banning the three media outlets for what he called "fake news" coverage. News organisations and press freedom groups have slammed the move as unconstitutional.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Millions without power in Cuba as electrical grid collapses again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a24192c871fcf581f0b7f668124fa62fc3767d0766abd5f2c874eeba25e6c71</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:01:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/millions-without-power-in-cuba-as-electrical-grid-collapses-again--8d09cc02680d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/millions-without-power-in-cuba-as-electrical-grid-collapses-again" /><summary type="html">Cuba was plunged into its seventh massive blackout of the year on Friday. The island of over nine million people endures constant power cuts due to the poor state of its aging thermoelectric plants – but the situation has worsened significantly since January, when Washington imposed a de facto energy blockade on the island. Story by Shirli Sitbon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump claims son repaid Russian oligarch who funded wedding festivities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8553cb790021f93dd7a97ab574975993c6fb31f72d5beee5fc25969692e7bcd0</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T10:26:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-trump-says-son-repaid-russian-oligarch-who-funded-wedding-festivities--ec19dbba0a0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-trump-says-son-repaid-russian-oligarch-who-funded-wedding-festivities" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday that his eldest son had repaid a Kremlin-linked Russian businessman who funded two days of lavish wedding celebrations in the Bahamas, after the gift raised questions over foreign influence and ethics.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump bans three media outlets from the White House, accusing them of spreading 'fake news'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c0d639bf0aa298d3b056d0580c3939edf673cc9078d5108c1f85032bb37ef8e</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:53:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-bans-three-media-outlets-from-the-white-house-accusing-them-of-spreading-fake-news--728977f11446.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-bans-three-media-outlets-from-the-white-house-accusing-them-of-spreading-fake-news" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump announced Friday he is banning CNN, MS NOW and Politico from the White House, accusing all three outlets of spreading 'fake news'. The move is almost certain to face legal challenges, and has been denounced by press freedom advocates. The US president's relationship with media outlets has long been fraught, as Charlotte Hughes explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Scientists discover first new wild cat in more than 100 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c8ee764e7173100762afa23e91d1a5cf350e22c57ab782e589631e5ffb66bf7</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:44:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-scientists-discover-first-new-wild-cat-in-more-than-100-years--a1fa381b5177.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-scientists-discover-first-new-wild-cat-in-more-than-100-years" /><summary type="html">Scientists have identified a previously unknown species of wild cat living at a wildlife sanctuary in Bolivia. The tiny, spotted feline had lived at the sanctuary for years before genetic analysis revealed it as the first new living wild cat species identified in more than a century.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Cuba hit with another nationwide blackout amid US fuel blockade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2457940d6f32ca4ce73ca7f9f5a995c45dd404d6d92600531fa0a09c007a7e1b</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:31:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cuba-s-power-grid-collapses-again-leaving-island-in-darkness--27a189638edf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cuba-s-power-grid-collapses-again-leaving-island-in-darkness" /><summary type="html">Cuba suffered a total blackout after the collapse of its electrical grid on Friday. The blackout is the latest of at least six partial or total grid collapses since the beginning of this year, as the island grapples with an ongoing US fuel blockade.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Pop star Ed Sheeran calls situation in Gaza 'unjustifiable' amid controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7872e74ddd941cfc4d16c3c371456cf763eb0ad1b172d693d319d946ab2d064b</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T05:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-situation-unjustifiable-amid-controversy" /><summary type="html">Ed Sheeran called the situation in Gaza “catastrophic and unjustifiable” on Saturday, speaking out for the first time since a controversy erupted over his tour’s removal of US rapper Macklemore after he made pro-Palestinian comments.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump bans media outlets CNN, MSNOW and Politico from the White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f4bcf5fe1ac4af1032030ddc916d58a574832813e91a2f75c6bbf7ff268305d</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:20:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260918-trump-bans-media-outlets-cnn-msnow-and-politico-from-white-house--abb8bd60e309.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260918-trump-bans-media-outlets-cnn-msnow-and-politico-from-white-house" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Friday said he would ban media outlets CNN, MSNOW and Politico from the White House over what he described as unfavourable coverage in his latest test of the US Constitution's First Amendment protection of press freedom.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>War in Iran 'jeopardises the Trump presidency', ex-Obama National Security Council member says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce98a48d677b97e2b6b0c9edceba8310d7488663daef6e38af874ed8de4406e8</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T17:01:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260918-war-in-iran-jeopardises-the-trump-presidency-ex-obama-national-security-council-member-says--08a330c92643.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260918-war-in-iran-jeopardises-the-trump-presidency-ex-obama-national-security-council-member-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, former Obama administration National Security Council member Charles Kupchan said the war in Iran "in many respects jeopardises the Trump presidency", calling it "yet another failed war of choice" that has driven up fuel and living costs ahead of the midterms. Trump's advisers "prize loyalty over fact", he added.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>A Sydney Sweeney ad goes viral: Are we all just being played?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcf2e93ff845f8ccbc26e8850026af69909eacc90598479071267e37d2d46762</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T16:27:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260918-sydney-sweeney-ad-goes-viral-are-we-all-just-being-played--40a2b8d26263.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260918-sydney-sweeney-ad-goes-viral-are-we-all-just-being-played" /><summary type="html">Another Sydney Sweeney ad goes viral – this time promoting a sports betting application almost naked. The campaign sparked fury among female athletes who said it undermines decades of progress in women's sports. Yet is the outrage itself part of the overall marketing strategy and ‘feminist-baiting’ merely a tool to get clicks?</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Fear and broken families: Inside a Texas ICE detention centre</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1aa70ba3a3756be52e4ab9ea7de78ccc7e9dbe467ce60bec6dfce5ec54778f45</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T08:26:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260918-reporters-fear-and-broken-families-inside-a-texas-ice-detention-centre--548ff42e0c58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260918-reporters-fear-and-broken-families-inside-a-texas-ice-detention-centre" /><summary type="html">Since Donald Trump’s return to the White House in January 2025, migrant arrests have surged in the United States. More than 610,000 people have passed through detention centres run by Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE), the federal immigration agency in under two years. The pace only continues to accelerate: in August 2026, nearly 51,000 arrests were made in a single month – a record for Trump’s second term. Who are the people being held in these centres? What are their living conditions like? And how is Trump’s mass deportation policy upending the lives of families settled in the United States? In this report, Valérie Defert and Pierrick Leurent investigate the issue in Texas – the heart of the new US immigration detention system.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Early voting begins in US midterms that could see Republicans lose control of Congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f51028d46b120891ea13abbacb0a59b51abbc475e96c358fd931a4aa24816046</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:15:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260918-early-voting-begins-in-us-midterms-that-could-see-republicans-lose-control-of-congress--90b2796051a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260918-early-voting-begins-in-us-midterms-that-could-see-republicans-lose-control-of-congress" /><summary type="html">In-person early voting for the US midterm elections begins Friday, six weeks ahead of the final November 3 vote, which will determine whether Republicans will maintain their majority in the US House and Senate. Some of the main issues American voters are deciding on are how to navigate the cost-of-living crisis, the war in Iran and President Donald Trump’s aggressive immigration enforcement campaign.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Rare Aztec manuscript returns to Mexico on loan after nearly two centuries in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:865528a432b3aea9d8ce64330f5c770bdc80e6e9f11664a6854a671ea86a6443</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T22:56:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260917-rare-aztec-manuscript-returns-to-mexico-on-loan-after-nearly-two-centuries-in-france--48ae560de03b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260917-rare-aztec-manuscript-returns-to-mexico-on-loan-after-nearly-two-centuries-in-france" /><summary type="html">A prized 16th-century manuscript chronicling the rise and fall of the Aztec Empire has gone on display in Mexico City, nearly two centuries after it was taken to France, as Mexico continues to press Paris for its permanent return.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Russian disinformation campaign targets Democrats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de885cabbf6e81050dfaa14eabca7f94273324008892db81d73ca0b1262d8864</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T21:19:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260917-us-midterms-russian-disinformation-campaign-targets-democrats--cfb73bd53905.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260917-us-midterms-russian-disinformation-campaign-targets-democrats" /><summary type="html">With US midterm elections now less than two months away, a series of videos have surfaced online, featuring celebrities seemingly denouncing the Democrats. However, the clips are fake, and were created using AI, as FRANCE 24's Charlotte Hughes explains.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>The Canada-EU partnership 'a classic win-win situation', economist says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:489ca367c6eaa0e59d138726f19a54a10f0ab5b9ef5ee6cc36da7e43fa775d5d</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T21:12:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260917-the-canada-eu-partnership-a-classic-win-win-situation-economist-says--9faf9f8ad86c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260917-the-canada-eu-partnership-a-classic-win-win-situation-economist-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Fabian Zuleeg, Chief Economist at the European Policy Center, says that the partnership between Canada and the EU "is a classic win-win situation – Canada has many resources, has many of the economic strengths that the European Union lacks, the EU has a very large market, it is an important trading partner".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>The Canada-EU partnership 'a classic win-win situation', economist says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdbce6ec3846fedf32e2dd18c0078c6311dfb897fdccc88e3d27cf6db124bee5</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T21:09:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-canada-eu-partnership-a-classic-win-win-situation-economist-says--8486820d185f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-canada-eu-partnership-a-classic-win-win-situation-economist-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Fabian Zuleeg, Chief Economist at the European Policy Center, says that the partnership between Canada and the EU "is a classic win-win situation – Canada has many resources, has many of the economic strengths that the European Union lacks, the EU has a very large market, it is an important trading partner".</summary></entry><entry><title>AFP photo shows Trump examining image of apparent Kennedy Center razing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a05974824028127b671fc138761dd88e576cd79c354b986f34e36ad29842e00</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T20:27:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/afp-photo-shows-trump-examining-image-of-apparent-kennedy-center-razing--836e56870e85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/afp-photo-shows-trump-examining-image-of-apparent-kennedy-center-razing" /><summary type="html">An AFP photo of Donald Trump examining a depiction of Washington's Kennedy Center apparently being demolished sparked widespread attention Thursday after the president threatened to tear down the revered arts venue because he has been blocked from renaming it after himself. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump threatens EU over 'hostile' Canada association plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc9fc8f4236cdae68589433dd7322c3ddedff4ca63da310bde67f14f70107a5f</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T20:04:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-threatens-eu-over-hostile-canada-association-plan--9f451de1a38b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-threatens-eu-over-hostile-canada-association-plan" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump threatened on Wednesday to cut trade with the European Union after the bloc proposed to make Canada its first ever associate member. "I think it's laughable," Trump told reporters when asked about the plan. "If they do that, if I think it's at all a hostile act, I will put very serious tariffs or stop trading with Europe, on many things." FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Guess who didn't like Mark Carney's speech today? The far-right'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcefcda3c3746dc23d1589c5e924e42c5e3700e69dbaec182ca5cd287a9a48d3</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T19:57:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/guess-who-didn-t-like-mark-carney-s-speech-today-the-far-right--a38f8e616aaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/guess-who-didn-t-like-mark-carney-s-speech-today-the-far-right" /><summary type="html">"There was thunderous applause for Mark Carney, a standing ovation, the centrist MEPs all loved him, the far-left MEPs also really liked it. But guess who didn't like this speech today? The far-right. Far-Right MEPs were grumbling about Mark Carney's presence and even when he started his speech one, a far-right MEP started chanting U-S-A! U-S-A!" FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports on Mark Carney's speech at the EU Parliament.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil election: Lula vows to stand up to Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8864c7fbd0989a46cdf71518efdfb14a280253450f4988bb92299b2c142b3eb7</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T14:47:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-election-lula-vows-to-stand-up-to-trump--465ca330fcf8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-election-lula-vows-to-stand-up-to-trump" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Lula says he will confront President Donald Trump at the UN in New York, accusing him of interfering in Brazil's election as tensions between Washington and Brasília deepen. The dispute comes after US tariffs on Brazilian goods and Trump's support for Lula's rival, Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of former president Jair Bolsonaro.</summary></entry><entry><title>US interest rate hike sparks Trump backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9659cab5f14d563393bdd1914eb7051701d26adf3e1914ffffbd849392a8a9a</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T14:21:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-interest-rate-hike-sparks-trump-backlash--482878a25184.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-interest-rate-hike-sparks-trump-backlash" /><summary type="html">The US Federal Reserve has raised interest rates for the first time since 2023, citing stubborn inflation despite pressure from President Donald Trump to cut borrowing costs. The decision prompted an immediate rebuke from Trump, while Fed Chair Kevin Warsh defended the central bank's independence and warned that inflation remains the priority.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mark Carney's EU speech highlights Canada's shifting alliances</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:028fecc8b5ef36bf3ef541c2f06ec22537cf7a38583a8bcb3f03b2a594b9433a</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:37:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mark-carney-s-eu-speech-highlights-canada-s-shifting-alliances-1--377245a8049c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mark-carney-s-eu-speech-highlights-canada-s-shifting-alliances-1" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney addressed the European Parliament as Ottawa and Brussels deepen ties against a backdrop of strained relations with the United States. FRANCE 24's Doug Herbert explains how the speech illustrates a broader shift in alliances, with a message that, until recently, would more likely have been delivered in Washington than Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Congress passes Russia sanctions bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f3beaab9b2c22d240122b7335f4c8916c1942b020ba29b4df18c41afb2dce52</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T10:26:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-congress-passes-russia-sanctions-bill--56b085a39b53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-congress-passes-russia-sanctions-bill" /><summary type="html">The US Congress has approved a sweeping Russia sanctions bill, sending it to President Donald Trump for final approval as Washington seeks to increase pressure on Moscow over the war in Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>US again denies Palestinian leader visa for UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16e0bebfcc1b6a35d4d893d579355486c8c497db412ee225dbcac28e19a09137</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T03:03:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260917-us-palestinian-leader-visa-un-general-assembly-new-york--07c18cfc3fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260917-us-palestinian-leader-visa-un-general-assembly-new-york" /><summary type="html">The United States has denied Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas a visa to attend next week's UN General Assembly in New York, a source familiar with the matter said on Wednesday. The State Department separately said it would deny visas to Palestinian officials, citing failures to reform and actions it said undermined peace prospects.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US House holds billionaire Epstein associate Leon Black in contempt of Congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81a924c9607c39deb0058bd0b02c76044cb512fcb7b565ce55061bee3fc6da6d</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T22:37:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-leon-black-epstein-contempt-congress--b3c6fcbe094a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-leon-black-epstein-contempt-congress" /><summary type="html">The US House of Representatives on Wednesday held billionaire investor Leon Black in contempt of Congress for defying two subpoenas in its investigation into sex offender Jeffrey Epstein. The measure passed by unanimous consent and will be referred to the Justice Department, which will decide whether to pursue criminal charges.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US announces charges against five alleged agents for Russia over assassination plots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad85815b628bf525ef6ee7afb7d9532f0cddf592f6ef6d2c428b14a9496a9a91</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:13:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-us-announces-charges-against-five-alleged-agents-for-russia-over-assassination-plots--d063e095b8a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-us-announces-charges-against-five-alleged-agents-for-russia-over-assassination-plots" /><summary type="html">The US Department of Justice announced on Tuesday charges against five alleged Russian intelligence agents accused of recruiting a global network to conspire attacks and carry out assassinations by order of the Kremlin. The suspects remain at large.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
